Subject: Preserve Fil-C capabilities across DPTR2FPTR/FPTR2DPTR and remaining Perl core ptrtable pairs
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: Project-authored core capability completeness patch covering 6 Perl 5.40.5 core locations where pointers were round-tripped through integers without preserving Fil-C capabilities: (1) perl.h:2536-2537 DPTR2FPTR/FPTR2DPTR previously cast via PTR2nat(p) (unsigned long), stripping function-pointer capabilities in op.c:14756,14847 (cv_get/set_call_checker_flags used by XS::APItest, Devel::Peek, IO, File::DosGlob, POSIX), sv.c:15368-15377 (thread destructor dup), and toke.c (source filters); replaced with direct ((t)(p)) casts; (2) op.c:15326,15406,15480 Perl_custom_op_register/get_field/free XOP* storage in PL_custom_ops routed via Perl_xsub_ptrtable; (3) op.c:4670 and op.h:858-860 Perl_blockhook_register/CALL_BLOCK_HOOKS BHK* storage routed via Perl_xsub_ptrtable; (4) mro_core.c:127,140 Perl_mro_register/get_from_name struct mro_alg* storage routed via Perl_xsub_ptrtable; (5) scope.c:1950,1977 Perl_mortal_svfunc_x/S_call_freedestruct SVFUNC_t storage routed via Perl_xsub_ptrtable; (6) op.c:1373,8714 and mg.c:2337 debugger breakpoint dbline COP* storage routed via Perl_xsub_ptrtable.
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none

--- a/perl.h
+++ b/perl.h
@@ -2535,8 +2535,8 @@
  * The only feasible use is probably temporarily storing
  * function pointers in a data pointer (such as a void pointer). */
 
-#define DPTR2FPTR(t,p) ((t)PTR2nat(p))	/* data pointer to function pointer */
-#define FPTR2DPTR(t,p) ((t)PTR2nat(p))	/* function pointer to data pointer */
+#define DPTR2FPTR(t,p) ((t)(p))	/* data pointer to function pointer */
+#define FPTR2DPTR(t,p) ((t)(p))	/* function pointer to data pointer */
 
 #ifdef USE_LONG_DOUBLE
 #  if LONG_DOUBLESIZE == DOUBLESIZE
--- a/op.h
+++ b/op.h
@@ -855,9 +855,9 @@
                 \
                 assert(SvIOK(sv)); \
                 if (SvUOK(sv)) \
-                    hk = INT2PTR(BHK *, SvUVX(sv)); \
+                    hk = (BHK *)zptrtable_decode(Perl_xsub_ptrtable, SvUVX(sv)); \
                 else \
-                    hk = INT2PTR(BHK *, SvIVX(sv)); \
+                    hk = (BHK *)zptrtable_decode(Perl_xsub_ptrtable, SvIVX(sv)); \
                 \
                 if (BhkENTRY(hk, which)) \
                     BhkENTRY(hk, which)(aTHX_ arg); \
